assertion  XCU.sh.001
anchor     utilities/sh.html#OPTIONS/Read commands from the <i>command_string</i> operand
anchor     utilities/sh.html#OPERANDS/command_name
class      required
says       sh -c runs the command string; command_name becomes $0 and the
           later operands $1, $2 ...; a string of several lines runs them in
           order.
test       t/001-dash-c.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.002
anchor     utilities/sh.html#OPERANDS/command_name
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.1.6
class      required
says       sh -c with no command_name sets $0 to the first argument the
           shell was started with, which for a command found by search is
           the command name.
test       t/002-dash-c-zero.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.003
anchor     utilities/sh.html#OPTIONS/No commands shall be
class      required
says       With -c the shell reads no commands from standard input, and the
           standard input stays available to the commands it runs.
test       t/003-dash-c-stdin.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.004
anchor     utilities/sh.html#OPTIONS/Read commands from the standard input
anchor     utilities/sh.html#OPERANDS/argument
class      required
says       sh -s reads commands from standard input and takes its operands
           as positional parameters; with no operands and no -c, -s is
           assumed.
test       t/004-dash-s.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.005
anchor     utilities/sh.html#OPERANDS/command_file
class      required
says       sh command_file argument... reads the commands from the file,
           which need not be executable, sets $0 to the file name as given
           and $1, $2 ... to the arguments; standard input is not read.
test       t/005-command-file.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.006
anchor     utilities/sh.html#OPERANDS/If the
anchor     utilities/sh.html#INPUT FILES/If the input file consists solely of
class      required
says       A command string, a file or standard input that holds only blank
           lines and comments (or nothing) makes sh exit with status zero.
test       t/006-empty-script.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.007
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXIT STATUS/the shell shall terminate in the same manner
class      required
says       sh ends with the status of the last command it ran (as exit with
           no operand does) or with the status given to exit.
test       t/007-exit-status.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.008
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXIT STATUS/could not be found by a non-interactive shell
class      required
says       sh with a command_file that does not exist exits with status 127.
test       t/008-file-not-found.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.009
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXIT STATUS/A non-interactive shell detected an error
class      required
says       A non-interactive sh that finds a syntax, redirection or variable
           assignment error exits with a status from 1 to 125.
test       t/009-error-status-range.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.010
anchor     utilities/sh.html#OPERANDS/treated as the first operand and then ignored
class      required
says       A single - operand is treated as the first operand and ignored.
test       t/010-single-hyphen.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.011
anchor     utilities/sh.html#OPTIONS/Utility Syntax Guidelines
class      required
says       sh accepts -- as the end of options, before the command string or
           the command file.
test       t/011-double-hyphen.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.012
anchor     utilities/sh.html#OPTIONS/described as part of the
class      required
says       Options given on the command line act as the same options of set,
           including the plus form that reverses one: -a, -C, -e, -f, -u
           (and -f followed by +f).
test       t/012-set-options.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.013
anchor     utilities/sh.html#OPTIONS/described as part of the
class      required
says       sh -n reads the commands but runs none, so a script is only
           syntax-checked: a good script gives status zero and no output; a
           script with a syntax error gives a non-zero status and a message.
test       t/013-noexec.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.014
anchor     utilities/sh.html#OPTIONS/described as part of the
class      required
says       sh -v and sh -x act as set -v and set -x: the input lines, or a
           trace of each expanded command, go to standard error.
test       t/014-trace-options.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.015
anchor     utilities/sh.html#OPTIONS/option-argument
class      required
since      2024
says       sh -o name and sh +o name act as set -o and set +o: noglob,
           errexit, nounset and pipefail are accepted.
test       t/015-long-options.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.016
anchor     utilities/sh.html#OPTIONS/Specify that the shell is <i>interactive</i>
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.5.2
class      required
says       sh -i makes the shell interactive, so "$-" contains i; a shell
           started without -i, with no terminal, is not interactive.
test       t/016-interactive-flag.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.017
anchor     utilities/sh.html#STDIN/It shall not read
class      required
says       When sh reads commands from standard input and runs a command
           that also reads standard input, the input is left just after the
           command line that started it: the shell has not read ahead.
test       t/017-no-read-ahead.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.018
anchor     utilities/sh.html#STDERR/standard error shall be used
class      required
says       sh writes to standard error only diagnostics: running good
           commands from a string, a file or standard input leaves standard
           error empty.
test       t/018-stderr-diagnostics-only.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.019
anchor     utilities/sh.html#INPUT FILES/shall not enforce any line length limits
class      required
says       sh accepts input lines of any length: a command line of 100000
           characters runs.
test       t/019-long-line.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.020
anchor     utilities/sh.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES/when and only when an interactive shell is invoked
class      conditional
when       UP
says       A non-interactive shell does not read the file named by ENV.
test       t/020-env-not-used.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.021
anchor     utilities/sh.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES/subjected to parameter expansion
class      conditional
when       UP
says       An interactive shell runs the file named by ENV, after parameter
           expansion of the value, in the current environment before reading
           its commands.
test       t/021-env-interactive.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.022
anchor     utilities/sh.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES/takes precedence over the
class      conditional
when       UP
says       An interactive shell with MAILPATH set and MAILCHECK zero informs the
           user, before a later prompt, with the message given for a file that
           has received mail.
timeout    60
test       t/022-mailpath-message.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.023
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/shall enable
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, typing the escape character puts the shell in command
           mode in which k brings the previous command line back for editing; the
           newline then runs it.
timeout    60
test       t/023-vi-mode-recall.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.024
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/shall enable
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, the escape character, a motion to the line start and x
           delete characters of the command line being edited, and the edited
           line is what runs.
timeout    60
test       t/024-vi-mode-delete-char.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.025
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Move the current cursor position to the next character position
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, in command mode the motions 0, ^, $, l, space, h
           and | (with counts) place the cursor so that a following r
           replaces the character there; a count larger than the line moves
           to the first or last character.
timeout    60
test       t/025-vi-char-motions.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.026
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Move to the start of the next bigword
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, the word motions w, W, b, B, e and E with counts
           move the cursor as defined for words and bigwords, a count past
           the end stopping at the last character.
timeout    60
test       t/026-vi-word-motions.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.027
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Repeat the most recent
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, f, F, t and T (with counts) and the repeats ; and
           , move to the named character in the stated direction.
timeout    60
test       t/027-vi-find-char.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.028
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Delete the character before the current cursor position
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, x and X delete the character at or before the
           cursor, D deletes to the end of the line, each into the save
           buffer, and p puts the save buffer after the cursor.
timeout    60
test       t/028-vi-delete-char-put.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.029
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Yank the characters from the current cursor position to the end of the line into the save buffer
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, d and y with a motion delete or copy text, d
           toward the line start leaves the cursor character, y leaves the
           cursor unchanged, and P puts the save buffer before the cursor.
timeout    60
test       t/029-vi-delete-yank-motion.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.030
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Delete from the current character to the end of the line and enter insert mode at the new end-of-line
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, c with a motion deletes the text and enters insert
           mode, and C changes to the end of the line.
timeout    60
test       t/030-vi-change.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.031
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Clear the entire edit line and enter insert mode
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, S and cc clear the whole edit line and enter
           insert mode.
timeout    60
test       t/031-vi-clear-line.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.032
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Enter insert mode, replacing characters from the command line beginning at the current cursor position
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, r with a count replaces that many characters
           leaving the cursor on the last changed one, and R replaces
           characters as they are typed.
timeout    60
test       t/032-vi-replace.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.033
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Enter insert mode at the beginning of the current command line
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, i, a, A and I enter insert mode before the cursor,
           after it, at the end and at the beginning of the line.
timeout    60
test       t/033-vi-insert-commands.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.034
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Convert, if the current
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, ~ converts the case of the character and advances
           the cursor, with a count converts that many, and a count past the
           end is not an error.
timeout    60
test       t/034-vi-tilde.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.035
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Repeat the most recent non-motion command, even if it was executed on an earlier command line
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, . repeats the most recent non-motion command; a
           count given to . replaces the old count and is kept for later
           repeats.
timeout    60
test       t/035-vi-dot-count.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.036
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Undo all changes made to the edit line
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, u undoes the last change to the edit line and U
           undoes all changes to it.
timeout    60
test       t/036-vi-undo.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.037
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Set the current command line to be the oldest command line stored in the shell command history
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, k with a count recalls an earlier command line and
           G without a number recalls the oldest command line in the history.
timeout    60
test       t/037-vi-history-k-G.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.038
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/next command line
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, j moves to the next command line in the history
           after k has moved back.
timeout    60
test       t/038-vi-history-j.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.039
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/previous command line
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, - and + move to the previous and next history
           lines, and - takes a count.
timeout    60
test       t/039-vi-history-minus-plus.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.040
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Move backwards through the command history, searching for the specified pattern
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, /pattern followed by a newline searches backward
           through the history and makes the found line the current line.
timeout    60
test       t/040-vi-search-backward.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.041
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Move forwards through the command history, searching for the specified pattern
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, ?pattern followed by a newline searches forward
           through the history.
timeout    60
test       t/041-vi-search-forward.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.042
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Repeat the most recent
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, n repeats the last history search in the same
           direction and N in the opposite direction.
timeout    60
test       t/042-vi-search-repeat.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.043
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Insert the character
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, # inserts a number sign at the start of the line,
           which is then treated as a comment and entered into the history.
timeout    60
test       t/043-vi-comment.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.044
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Display the possible shell word expansions
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, = displays the pathname expansions of the bigword
           at the cursor on later lines, adding a slash to directories,
           without changing the line.
timeout    60
test       t/044-vi-expand-display.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.045
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Perform pathname expansion on the current bigword and insert all expansions into the command to replace the current bigword
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, * replaces the bigword at the cursor by all its
           pathname expansions separated by spaces.
timeout    60
test       t/045-vi-expand-insert.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.046
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Perform pathname expansion (see
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, a backslash completes the bigword at the cursor to
           the unique match and enters insert mode.
timeout    60
test       t/046-vi-expand-complete.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.047
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Insert the value of the alias named
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, @ followed by a letter inserts the value of the
           alias named with an underscore and that letter.
timeout    60
test       t/047-vi-alias-insert.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.048
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Redraw the current command line
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, control-L redraws the line and leaves the cursor
           at the same place.
timeout    60
test       t/048-vi-redraw.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.049
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Append a
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, _ appends a space and the last bigword of the
           previous input line, or with a count the numbered bigword.
timeout    60
test       t/049-vi-underscore.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.050
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Put a copy of the current contents of the save buffer after the current cursor position
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, Y yanks to the end of the line and a count on p
           puts that many copies after the cursor.
timeout    60
test       t/050-vi-yank-put-count.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.051
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/yanked into the save buffer
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, yy yanks the whole line leaving the cursor, p puts
           it after the cursor, and dd clears the line.
timeout    60
test       t/051-vi-yy-dd.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.052
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/SIGINT signal in command
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, an interrupt typed in insert or command mode
           abandons the line and the abandoned line is not entered in the
           history.
timeout    60
test       t/052-vi-interrupt.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.053
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Clear all the characters from the input line
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, in insert mode the erase character removes the
           previous character and the kill character clears the line.
timeout    60
test       t/053-vi-erase-kill.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.054
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Delete the characters from the one preceding the cursor to the preceding word boundary
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, in insert mode control-W deletes the word before
           the cursor.
timeout    60
test       t/054-vi-word-erase.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.055
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Insert the next character input, even if the character is otherwise a special insert mode character
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, in insert mode control-V inserts the next
           character even if it is the kill character.
timeout    60
test       t/055-vi-literal-next.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.056
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Interpreted as the end
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, the end-of-file character at the beginning of a
           line ends the shell.
timeout    60
test       t/056-vi-eof.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.057
anchor     utilities/sh.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/temporary file
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi, v in command mode invokes vi on the current
           command line in a temporary file, and when vi exits the commands
           in the file are executed.
timeout    60
test       t/057-vi-edit-command.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.058
anchor     utilities/sh.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES/Determine a pathname naming a command history file
class      conditional
when       UP
says       The command history kept in the file named by HISTFILE survives
           between interactive sessions: a command typed in one session is
           listed by fc -l in a later session that uses the same file.
timeout    60
test       t/058-histfile-persist.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.059
anchor     utilities/sh.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES/Determine a pathname naming a command history file
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With set -o vi in a later session using the same HISTFILE, k with
           a count recalls a command typed in an earlier session.
timeout    60
test       t/059-histfile-recall.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.060
anchor     utilities/sh.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES/takes precedence over the
class      conditional
when       UP
says       When MAILPATH and MAIL are both set, only the files of MAILPATH
           are watched: a change to the MAIL file adds nothing to what the
           user is told.
timeout    60
test       t/060-mail-precedence.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.061
anchor     utilities/sh.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES/Determine a pathname of the user
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With MAIL set and MAILPATH unset, the shell informs the user,
           before a later prompt, when the MAIL file is created.
timeout    60
test       t/061-mail-default.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.062
anchor     utilities/sh.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES/Establish a decimal integer value that specifies how often
class      conditional
when       UP
says       The shell checks for mail only after the MAILCHECK interval since
           the last check: a change made soon after a check is reported only
           at a prompt after the interval has passed.
timeout    60
test       t/062-mailcheck-interval.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.063
anchor     utilities/sh.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES/preceded by a
class      conditional
when       UP
says       In MAILPATH a percent sign preceded by a backslash belongs to the
           pathname.
timeout    60
test       t/063-mailpath-percent.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.064
anchor     utilities/sh.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES/a string that shall be subjected to parameter expansion
class      conditional
when       UP
says       The message of a MAILPATH entry undergoes parameter expansion when
           it is written.
timeout    60
test       t/064-mailpath-expand.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.065
anchor     utilities/sh.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES/Provide a list of pathnames and optional messages separated by
class      conditional
when       UP
says       MAILPATH names several files separated by colons and the message
           of the file that changed is the one written.
timeout    60
test       t/065-mailpath-multiple.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.066
anchor     utilities/sh.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES/If set to zero, the shell shall
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With MAILCHECK zero the shell checks before each primary prompt,
           so two later changes are reported separately.
timeout    60
test       t/066-mailcheck-zero.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.067
anchor     utilities/sh.html#ASYNCHRONOUS EVENTS/SIGTTIN, SIGTTOU, and SIGTSTP signals shall be ignored
class      conditional
when       UP
says       With the -m option in effect the shell ignores SIGTSTP, SIGTTIN
           and SIGTTOU sent to itself.
timeout    60
test       t/067-monitor-ignores-stop.sh

assertion  XCU.sh.068
anchor     utilities/sh.html#ASYNCHRONOUS EVENTS/SIGQUIT and SIGTERM signals shall be ignored
class      conditional
when       UP
says       An interactive shell ignores SIGTERM and SIGQUIT sent to itself.
timeout    60
test       t/068-ignores-term-quit.sh
